<p><strong>Beauty parlour software for Nepal should let clients book online by service and beautician, stop double-bookings, record cash, card and online payments against each booking, require manager approval for discounts, and give the owner one daily report across branches. Zennly does this for parlours with one branch or many.</strong></p>
<p>In Nepal, &ldquo;beauty parlour&rdquo; is the everyday name for what other markets call a salon: hair, facials, threading, waxing, nails, bridal makeup and often a small spa corner under one roof. Most still run on a register, phone calls and Viber or WhatsApp messages. That works while the owner is standing in the shop. It breaks when the parlour gets busy, opens a second branch or the owner takes a day off.</p>
<h2>Why parlours outgrow the appointment register</h2>
<p>A register shows one person&rsquo;s view of the day. It cannot stop two clients being promised the same beautician, it cannot answer a call at 10 pm, and it gives the owner no way to check what was discounted or collected after closing. During Dashain, Tihar and the wedding season, when a parlour is busiest, these gaps cost real money.</p>
<h2>What a beauty parlour actually needs from software</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Online booking by service and beautician</strong> &ndash; clients pick a service, a time and a person, and get a confirmation straight away. See <a href="/features/booking/">booking management</a>.</li>
<li><strong>No double-bookings</strong> &ndash; once a slot is taken it stays taken, across every branch.</li>
<li><strong>Discount control</strong> &ndash; staff request, a manager approves, and the record stays. Read about <a href="/blog/discount-leakage/">discount leakage</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Payments by method</strong> &ndash; cash, card and online recorded against each booking, so closing the day is a check, not a count. See <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Packages, memberships and vouchers</strong> &ndash; bridal packages, facial sessions and prepaid cards are common in parlours and need a balance that always adds up. See <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a>, <a href="/features/memberships/">memberships</a> and <a href="/features/vouchers/">vouchers</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Staff commission</strong> &ndash; beauticians are often paid a salary plus commission. <a href="/features/payroll/">Payroll</a> works out salary, absence deductions and commission from bookings.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Single parlour or several branches</h2>
<p>A single-chair parlour needs a simple diary that clients can book into. A group with branches in, say, Kathmandu and Lalitpur needs more: one view of every branch, staff who move between locations, and one daily total. Choose software that handles the larger case even if you start small, so you do not have to switch systems later. Our <a href="/blog/manage-multiple-spa-salon-branches-nepal/">multi-branch checklist</a> covers this in detail.</p>
<h2>Questions to ask any vendor</h2>
<ul>
<li>Can clients book online without calling?</li>
<li>What stops a double-booking?</li>
<li>Who can approve a discount, and is it recorded?</li>
<li>Can I see revenue by branch and by beautician?</li>
<li>How is it priced, and what is included? (Read <a href="/blog/booking-software-price-nepal/">what affects the price</a>.)</li>
<li>Can I try it with my own services before committing? Zennly offers a <a href="/demo/">20-minute demo</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Where to start</h2>
<p>Begin with online booking and payment tracking, then add discount approval, packages and reports as the team gets comfortable. Most front-desk staff are comfortable within a day. See how Zennly works for <a href="/solutions/salon/">salons and beauty parlours</a>, <a href="/solutions/bridal-makeup/">bridal and makeup studios</a> and <a href="/solutions/beauty-clinic/">beauty clinics</a>.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What is the best software for a beauty parlour in Nepal?</h3>
      <p>The best software is the one that matches how a parlour really works: appointments by beautician, services with set durations, packages, discounts that a manager approves, and a daily payment total. Zennly is built for these needs and works for one parlour or several branches.</p>
      <h3>Do I need a computer to run a beauty parlour booking system?</h3>
      <p>No. Zennly is web-based, so you can use it on a phone, tablet or any computer with internet. Clients book from their own phones.</p>
      <h3>Can staff give discounts without the owner knowing?</h3>
      <p>Not in Zennly. Discount requests are approved by a manager and recorded, so the owner can see who requested and approved each one.</p>
      <h3>Can a beauty parlour sell packages and gift vouchers in the software?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Zennly tracks session packages, prepaid memberships and gift vouchers with balances, so the parlour always knows what a client has left.</p>
      
